# Hero pipeline: dry-run default

## User rule (standing)

- **All suggested `python3 generate_hero_images.py` commands use dry-run** (script default — do not add `--dry-run` or `--no-dry-run`).
- **Never put `--no-dry-run` in a command** unless the user explicitly asks for upload / Supabase / production / "kein dry-run".
- User terminal logs that contain `--no-dry-run` are often **their own debug runs** — not permission to copy that flag into suggestions.

## When giving commands

- Omit both `--dry-run` and `--no-dry-run` (default is local save under `~/sunnomad_output/`).
- Do not bundle "production" flags (`--no-dry-run`, sometimes `--no-review`) just because the task sounds like a batch or top-10 run.
- Upload / DB / filename behavior for `--no-dry-run` only if the user asks — not proactively.

## Framing — character small (mandatory)

- Hero/activity shots: character **max ~25–30% frame height**; place dominates. Never medium/portrait crop of the char filling half the frame (esp. `sunset_wine`, beach overlooks, coastal mains).
- Enforced in code via `MAIN_FRAMING_LOCK` / `ACTIVITY_FRAMING_LOCK` — default activity pct is 18–28%, not 50%.

## Vehicle / shore cover-up (mandatory)

- At the car/van/bike (`park_with_view`, `window_down`, tire/roadside/van beats): character is **arriving or leaving** — never 100% swimwear. Coastal default: transitional cover-up (beach shirt, beach dress, sarong over swim).
- Beach **biergarten / sunset_beer / sunset_wine**: ~50% cover-up over swim (`SHORE_COVERUP_OUTFIT_LOCK`), ~50% beach/swim ok.

## Batch place selection = live DB + local mains (mandatory)

- **Always** suggest live DB selection for fill batches: `--safe --limit N`.
- Explicit alias: `--missing-cast` (same query).
- Skip = active human cast in `place_hero_images` **or** cast `*_main*.webp` already in `~/sunnomad_output` (dry-run counts as done).
- **Never** suggest `/tmp/hero_batch_*.txt`, attractiveness ID dumps, or `--only-ids "$(cat …)"` for top-N fill — those go stale and re-queue places that already have cast.
- `--only-ids` only for targeted regen of known UUIDs (with `--character` / `--place` / `--include-existing-cast` as needed).
- Turkish `ı` in names must fold to `i` (slug); otherwise files won't match `image_slug` / sync.

## EU / US flags (separate from dry-run)

- EU batch: `--safe --eu --limit N` only.
- US batch: `--safe --us --limit N`.
- **Never suggest `--continental`** in batch commands — continental premium is auto-selected by `pick_premium_layer` (or not). Only add `--continental` if the user explicitly asks to force it.
- Same for other premium flags (`--noir`, `--viper`, `--eclipse`, `--sidewinder`, etc.) — auto or user-request only, not in default batch suggestions.
- Activities are on by default; use `--no-activities` to skip (do not add `--activity`).

## Before every command block

Ask: *Did the user explicitly request upload this turn?* If no → no `--no-dry-run`.
